            <ArticleTitle>Discovery and evaluation of spirocyclic derivatives as antagonists of the neuropeptide Y5 receptor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2738-43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2012.02.098</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel series of spirocyclic derivatives was synthesized and evaluated as NPY Y5R antagonists for the treatment of obesity. Cis and trans analogs 7a and 8a were equipotent in a Y5R binding assay (K(i)'s ≤ 1 nM) and displayed good stability in human and rat liver microsome preparations. Compound 7a failed to demonstrate weight loss activity in a diet-induced obese (DIO) rat model at unbound drug levels in the brain that exceeded the Y5R K(i) value by 25-fold over a 24-h time-period.</AbstractText>
